    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.clue\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nFirst of all thanks for making mini.nvim! It is an awesome collection of lightweight but functional modules.\r\n\r\nI am currently considering adding mini.clue to my workflow to help me remember some less-used keymaps, mainly debug keymaps and buffer-local keymaps defined by plugins. However, mini.nvim does not show buffer-local keymaps for me.\r\n\r\nFor example, oil.nvim defines some buffer-local keymaps for opening files using external program, reorder files, toggle preview, etc with `g` as prefix. When I press `g` in a oil buffer, mini.clue does not show up. I've also tried which-key.nvim and it works as expected in this case.\r\n\r\nOil.nvim's buffer-local keymaps:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cf116638-cf18-4664-892f-4ad171591683)\r\n\r\nWith mini.clue:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f08c8dea-a0e1-4c85-a9a4-24e544f7f3aa)\r\n\r\nWith which-key.nvim:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e678c89d-4811-47ef-a70c-cd454ab36044)\r\n",
