            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the kind words!\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce the behavior with plain `require('oil').setup()` and [full starter setup of 'mini.clue'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c520765241541e0c7d4bc6fd4a716f706b0d5de7/doc/mini-clue.txt#L236) . It works as expected: pressing `g` shows *all* available mappings (both global and buffer-local from 'oil.nvim') plus possibly additional clues (as a result of [`gen_clues.g()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c520765241541e0c7d4bc6fd4a716f706b0d5de7/doc/mini-clue.txt#L278)). 'mini.clue' already supports buffer-local mappings, so this shouldn't be the culprit of the issue.\r\n\r\nDoes `g` trigger work in regular buffers (pressing `g` and waiting 1 second should show available Normal mode mappings that start with `g`)? With 'oil.nvim' buffer being current, does `:nmap g` show an entry from 'mini.clue' with description \"Query keys after \"g\"\"?",
